mate gets a free play, which is ideal. If the landlord plays a joker, they\'ve burned a premium card.\n\nReason:\nI should pass because my teammate\'s ♦2 is already an extremely strong play that puts maximum pressure on the landlord. Playing my BlackJoker or bomb would be wasteful when my teammate\'s card is likely to win this trick anyway. By passing, I preserve my strongest cards for when they\'re truly needed, and allow my teammate to potentially regain control of the game with a free play if the landlord passes.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
